2025-10-16 20:51:39,626 - INFO -  - YT3yZnqTbCxFPYsM - -  hAuD8ioT5CD2uqqE - - D:\miniconda\envs\datamining\Lib\site-packages\oxygent\oxy\base_oxy.py line:437 - user <<< master <<< analyser <<< http_agent <<< qwen  : <think>The README.md file has been successfully retrieved from the GitHub repository. It contains detailed information about Dify, including its features, installation instructions, community links, and more. I can now summarize the key points for the user.</think>
Dify is an open-source platform designed for developing LLM (Large Language Model) applications. It offers a user-friendly interface that supports AI workflows, RAG pipelines, agent capabilities, model management, and observability features, enabling rapid development from prototype to production.

Key Features:
- **Workflow**: Build and test AI workflows visually.
- **Model Support**: Integrates with hundreds of LLMs from various providers, including GPT, Mistral, Llama3, and OpenAI-compatible models.
- **Prompt IDE**: Craft prompts and compare model performance with added functionalities like text-to-speech.
- **RAG Pipeline**: Supports document ingestion and retrieval, with built-in extraction from formats like PDFs and PPTs.
- **Agent Capabilities**: Create agents using LLM Function Calling or ReAct, enhanced with over 50 pre-built tools (e.g., Google Search, DALL·E).
- **LLMOps**: Monitor application logs and improve models based on real-world data.
- **Backend-as-a-Service**: Full API access for seamless integration into custom business logic.

Getting Started:
You can use Dify via:
- **Dify Cloud**: A hosted version available at [https://cloud.dify.ai](https://cloud.dify.ai) with free GPT-4 calls in the sandbox plan.
- **Self-hosting**: Deploy locally using Docker Compose after installing Docker and Docker Compose.
- **Enterprise Use**: Contact via email or chatbot for enterprise-specific features.

Community & Support:
- GitHub Discussions and Issues for feedback and bug reports.
- Discord and X (Twitter) for community interaction.
- Translation contributions are welcome for non-Mandarin/English speakers.

For more details, visit the [documentation](https://docs.dify.ai) or explore the project on [GitHub](https://github.com/langgenius/dify).
