st.ini](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent/blob/main/pytest.ini \"pytest.ini\") | [feat: init](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent/commit/ab0010a5256f6a478bcf4e797d6c74c075b6886a \"feat: init\") | 3 months agoJul 21, 2025 |\n| [requirements.txt](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent/blob/main/requirements.txt \"requirements.txt\") | [requirements.txt](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent/blob/main/requirements.txt \"requirements.txt\") | [add requests](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent/commit/ba52ecb6176b92576a07893b6b15c06f3fa62276 \"add requests\") | last monthSep 22, 2025 |\n| View all files |\n\n## Repository files navigation\n\n[English](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent/blob/main/README.md) \\| [中文](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent/blob/main/README_zh.md)\n\n[![PRs Welcome](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/88482ebfc5e3e4f2d667148ab6a3eb55948789f1dba71dfa0eb2e05afe02958c/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f5052732d77656c636f6d652d627269676874677265656e2e7376673f7374796c653d666c61742d737175617265)](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent/pulls)[![license](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/5ce2e21e84680df1ab24807babebc3417d27d66e0826a350eb04ab57f4c8f3e5/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f4c6963656e73652d4170616368655f322e302d626c75652e737667)](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent/blob/v4/LICENSE)[![pip](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/7fea4b9463f0e3f81920a4fdabc52d0d430bc61f16bb2343fdccc755c670a891/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f707970692f762f6f787967656e742e7376673f6c6f676f3d70797069266c6f676f436f6c6f723d7768697465)](https://pypi.org/project/oxygent/)\n\n## [![](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/fd9ea116979458696c3c26b429482471eb5c94febf9e5878cda78c271cfecd4e/68747470733a2f2f73746f726167652e6a642e636f6d2f61692d676174657761792d726f7574696e672f70726f645f646174612f6f787967656e745f6769746875625f696d616765732f62616e6e65722e6a7067)](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/fd9ea116979458696c3c26b429482471eb5c94febf9e5878cda78c271cfecd4e/68747470733a2f2f73746f726167652e6a642e636f6d2f61692d676174657761792d726f7574696e672f70726f645f646174612f6f787967656e745f6769746875625f696d616765732f62616e6e65722e6a7067)\n\n[Permalink: ](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#----------)\n\n### An advanced Python framework that empowers developers to quickly build production-ready intelligent systems.\n\n[Permalink:\\\n      An advanced Python framework that empowers developers to quickly build production-ready intelligent systems.\\\n    ](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#------an-advanced-python-framework-that-empowers-developers-to-quickly-build-production-ready-intelligent-systems-----)\n\n### Visit our website:  [OxyGent](http://oxygent.jd.com/)\n\n[Permalink:\\\n      Visit our website:\\\n      OxyGent](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#------visit-our-website------oxygent----)\n\n## 1\\. Project Overview\n\n[Permalink: 1. Project Overview](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#1-project-overview)\n\n**OxyGent** is an open-source framework that unifies tools, models, and agents into modular Oxy. Empowering developers with transparent, end-to-end pipelines, OxyGent makes building, running, and evolving multi-agent systems seamless and infinitely extensible.\n\n## 2\\. Core Features\n\n[Permalink: 2. Core Features](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#2-core-features)\n\n🏎️ **Efficient Development**\n\n- OxyGent is a modular multi-agent framework that lets you build, deploy, and evolve AI teams with unprecedented efficiency. Its standardized Oxy components snap together like LEGO bricks, enabling rapid assembly of agents while supporting hot-swapping and cross-scenario reuse - all through clean Python interfaces without messy configs.\n\n🤝 **Intelligent Collaboration**\n\n- The framework supercharges collaboration with dynamic planning paradigms, where agents intelligently decompose tasks, negotiate solutions, and adapt to changes in real-time. Unlike rigid workflow systems, OxyGent's agents handle emergent challenges naturally while maintaining full auditability of every decision.\n\n🕸️ **Elastic Architecture**\n\n- Under the hood, an elastic architecture supports any agent topology- from simple ReAct to complex hybrid planning patterns. Automated dependency mapping and visual debugging tools make it easy to optimize performance across distributed systems.\n\n🔁 **Continuous Evolution**\n\n- Every interaction becomes a learning opportunity - thanks to built-in evaluation engines that auto-generate training data. Your agents continuously improve through knowledge feedback loops while maintaining full transparency.\n\n📈 **Scalability**\n\n- Scaling follows Metcalfe's Law- OxyGent's distributed scheduler enables linear cost growth while delivering exponential gains in collaborative intelligence. The system effortlessly handles domain-wide optimization and real-time decision making at any scale.\n\nThe latest version of OxyGent (July 15, 2025) in the [GAIA](https://huggingface.co/spaces/gaia-benchmark/leaderboard) get 59.14 points, and current top opensource system OWL gets 60.8 points.\n\n[![](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/a30069ec3719550095a62de263c66ce720283b6070c69ee124ff61f79ea1fdbb/68747470733a2f2f73746f726167652e6a642e636f6d2f61692d676174657761792d726f7574696e672f70726f645f646174612f6f787967656e745f6769746875625f696d616765732f706f696e74732e706e67)](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/a30069ec3719550095a62de263c66ce720283b6070c69ee124ff61f79ea1fdbb/68747470733a2f2f73746f726167652e6a642e636f6d2f61692d676174657761792d726f7574696e672f70726f645f646174612f6f787967656e745f6769746875625f696d616765732f706f696e74732e706e67)\n\n## 3\\. Framework Core Classes\n\n[Permalink: 3. Framework Core Classes](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#3-framework-core-classes)\n\n[![](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/b5c9a8c1bec12848a79ed75aadfa97febc9ec704484a3fc792a00a4329732431/68747470733a2f2f73746f726167652e6a642e636f6d2f61692d676174657761792d726f7574696e672f70726f645f646174612f6f787967656e745f6769746875625f696d616765732f7374727563747572652e706e67)](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/b5c9a8c1bec12848a79ed75aadfa97febc9ec704484a3fc792a00a4329732431/68747470733a2f2f73746f726167652e6a642e636f6d2f61692d676174657761792d726f7574696e672f70726f645f646174612f6f787967656e745f6769746875625f696d616765732f7374727563747572652e706e67)\n\n## 4\\. Feature Highlight\n\n[Permalink: 4. Feature Highlight](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#4-feature-highlight)\n\n**For Developers**: Focus on business logic without reinventing the wheel.\n\n**For Enterprises**: Replace siloed AI systems with a unified framework, reducing communication overhead.\n\n**For Users**: Experience seamless teamwork from an intelligent agent ecosystem.\n\n## 5\\. Quick Start\n\n[Permalink: 5. Quick Start](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#5-quick-start)\n\n### Step 1: Create and activate a python environment\n\n[Permalink: Step 1: Create and activate a python environment](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#step-1-create-and-activate-a-python-environment)\n\n- Method 1: conda\n\n\n\n```\nconda create -n oxy_env python==3.10\nconda activate oxy_env\n```\n\n- Method 2: uv\n\n\n\n```\ncurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh\nuv python install 3.10\nuv venv .venv --python 3.10\nsource .venv/bin/activate\n```\n\n\n### Step 2: Install the required python package\n\n[Permalink: Step 2: Install the required python package](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#step-2-install-the-required-python-package)\n\n- Method 1: conda\n\n\n\n```\npip install oxygent\n```\n\n- Method 2: uv\n\n\n\n```\nuv pip install oxygent\n```\n\n- Method 3: set develop environment\n\n\n\n```\ngit clone https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent.git\ncd OxyGent\npip install -r requirements.txt # or in uv\nbrew install coreutils # maybe essential\n```\n\n\n### Step 3: Node.js Environment (if using MCP)\n\n[Permalink: Step 3: Node.js Environment (if using MCP)](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#step-3-nodejs-environment-if-using-mcp)\n\n- Download and install **[Node.js](https://nodejs.org/)**\n\n### Step 4: Write a sample python script\n\n[Permalink: Step 4: Write a sample python script](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#step-4-write-a-sample-python-script)\n\n- demo.py\n\n\n\n```\nimport os\nfrom oxygent import MAS, Config, oxy, preset_tools\n\nConfig.set_agent_llm_model(\"default_llm\")\n\noxy_space = [\\\n     oxy.HttpLLM(\\\n        name=\"default_llm\",\\\n        api_key=os.getenv(\"DEFAULT_LLM_API_KEY\"),\\\n        base_url=os.getenv(\"DEFAULT_LLM_BASE_URL\"),\\\n        model_name=os.getenv(\"DEFAULT_LLM_MODEL_NAME\"),\\\n     ),\\\n     preset_tools.time_tools,\\\n     oxy.ReActAgent(\\\n        name=\"time_agent\",\\\n        desc=\"A tool that can query the time\",\\\n        tools=[\"time_tools\"],\\\n     ),\\\n     preset_tools.file_tools,\\\n     oxy.ReActAgent(\\\n        name=\"file_agent\",\\\n        desc=\"A tool that can operate the file system\",\\\n        tools=[\"file_tools\"],\\\n     ),\\\n     preset_tools.math_tools,\\\n     oxy.ReActAgent(\\\n        name=\"math_agent\",\\\n        desc=\"A tool that can perform mathematical calculations.\",\\\n        tools=[\"math_tools\"],\\\n     ),\\\n     oxy.ReActAgent(\\\n        is_master=True,\\\n        name=\"master_agent\",\\\n        sub_agents=[\"time_agent\", \"file_agent\", \"math_agent\"],\\\n     ),\\\n]\n\nasync def main():\n     async with MAS(oxy_space=oxy_space) as mas:\n        await mas.start_web_service(\n           first_query=\"What time is it now? Please save it into time.txt.\"\n        )\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n     import asyncio\n     asyncio.run(main())\n```\n\n\n### Step 5: Set Environment Variables\n\n[Permalink: Step 5: Set Environment Variables](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#step-5-set-environment-variables)\n\n- Method 1: Declare in terminal\n\n\n\n```\nexport DEFAULT_LLM_API_KEY=\"your_api_key\"\nexport DEFAULT_LLM_BASE_URL=\"your_base_url\"\nexport DEFAULT_LLM_MODEL_NAME=\"your_model_name\"\n```\n\n- Method 2: Create a .env file\n\n\n\n```\nDEFAULT_LLM_API_KEY=\"your_api_key\"\nDEFAULT_LLM_BASE_URL=\"your_base_url\"\nDEFAULT_LLM_MODEL_NAME=\"your_model_name\"\n```\n\n\n### Step 6: Run the example\n\n[Permalink: Step 6: Run the example](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#step-6-run-the-example)\n\n- Start the multi-agent system\n\n\n\n```\npython demo.py\n```\n\n\n### Step 7: View the output\n\n[Permalink: Step 7: View the output](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#step-7-view-the-output)\n\n- [![](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/ce821072f8851cdc96655cb09bb2c114a8e4b350dc3621822593fe31c3e19973/68747470733a2f2f73746f726167652e6a642e636f6d2f61692d676174657761792d726f7574696e672f70726f645f646174612f6f787967656e745f6769746875625f696d616765732f766973696f6e2e706e67)](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/ce821072f8851cdc96655cb09bb2c114a8e4b350dc3621822593fe31c3e19973/68747470733a2f2f73746f726167652e6a642e636f6d2f61692d676174657761792d726f7574696e672f70726f645f646174612f6f787967656e745f6769746875625f696d616765732f766973696f6e2e706e67)\n\n## 6\\. Contributing\n\n[Permalink: 6. Contributing](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#6-contributing)\n\nThere are several ways you can contribute to OxyGent:\n\n1. Reporting Issues (Bugs & Errors)\n2. Suggesting Enhancements\n3. Improving Documentation\n   - Fork the repository\n   - Add your view in document\n   - Send your pull request\n4. Writing Code\n   - Fork the repository\n   - Create a new branch\n   - Add your feature or improvement\n   - Send your pull request\n\nWe appreciate all kinds of contributions! 🎉🎉🎉\nIf you have problems about development, please check our document: \\* **[Document](http://oxygent.jd.com/docs/)**\n\n## 7\\. Community & Support\n\n[Permalink: 7. Community & Support](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#7-community--support)\n\nIf you encounter any issues along the way, you are welcomed to submit reproducible steps and log snippets in the project's Issues area, or contact the OxyGent Core team directly via your internal Slack.\n\nWelcome to contact us:\n\n[![contact](https://camo.githubusercontent.)](https://camo.githubusercontent.)\n\n## 8\\. About the Contributors\n\n[Permalink: 8. About the Contributors](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#8-about-the-contributors)\n\nThanks to all the following [developers](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent/graphs/contributors) who have contributed to OxyGent.\n[![](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/efcce9cdff8558f982eac0c847a4801b75bc92a1e0c5337f80c53960e7ae15a0/68747470733a2f2f636f6e747269622e726f636b732f696d6167653f7265706f3d6a642d6f70656e736f757263652f4f787947656e74)](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent/graphs/contributors)\n\n## 9\\. License\n\n[Permalink: 9. License](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#9-license)\n\n[Apache License](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent/blob/main/LICENSE.md)\n\n#### OxyGent is provided by Oxygen JD.com\n\n[Permalink: OxyGent is provided by Oxygen JD.com](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#oxygent-is-provided-by-oxygen-jdcom)\n\n#### Thanks for your Contributions!\n\n[Permalink: Thanks for your Contributions!](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#thanks-for-your-contributions)\n\n## About\n\nMulti-agent collaboration framework\n\n\n[oxygent.jd.com](https://oxygent.jd.com/ \"https://oxygent.jd.com\")\n\n### Resources\n\n[Readme](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#readme-ov-file)\n\n### License\n\n[View license](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#License-1-ov-file)\n\n### Contributing\n\n[Contributing](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#contributing-ov-file)\n\n### Security policy\n\n[Security policy](https://github.com/jd-opensource/OxyGent#security-ov-file)\n\n### Uh oh!\n\nThere was an error while loading. [Please reload this page